    "assumptions": [
      "Stereo elements: tetrahedral centers (R/S, pseudoasymmetric r/s) and double bonds (E/Z), as perceived by RDKit.",
      "Relations: an isomer's mirror image has every tetrahedral center inverted; isomers are compared by canonical SMILES.",
      "meso: an achiral stereoisomer (it has stereocenters but is identical to its mirror image) in a set that also contains chiral stereoisomers (IUPAC Gold Book). Achiral isomers in a set without chiral members, such as cis- and trans-1,4-dimethylcyclohexane, are called achiral.",
      "3D: one conformer per isomer (ETKDGv3, fixed seed), optimized with MMFF94. Energies belong to that conformer, not to the lowest-energy conformer, so they are not reliable for comparing diastereomers. The second isomer of an enantiomer pair is the mirror image of the first (same energy)."
    ],
    "sources": [
      "RDKit 2026.09.1: stereoisomer enumeration, new CIP labeler (R. M. Hanson et al., J. Chem. Inf. Model. 2018, 58, 1755–1765), ETKDGv3 (S. Wang, J. Witek, G. A. Landrum, S. Riniker, J. Chem. Inf. Model. 2020, 60, 2044–2058), MMFF94 (T. A. Halgren, J. Comput. Chem. 1996, 17, 490–519).",
      "IUPAC numbering: H. A. Favre, W. H. Powell, Nomenclature of Organic Chemistry: IUPAC Recommendations and Preferred Names 2013, Royal Society of Chemistry, 2014 (P-31.1.4, P-44).",
      "meso: IUPAC Compendium of Chemical Terminology (Gold Book), 'meso-compound', https://doi.org/10.1351/goldbook.M03839."
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Relations: E = enantiomers, D = diastereomers.",
      "Numbers in the stereodescriptors are IUPAC locants of the parent (4-carbon chain), IUPAC 2013 Recommendations P-31.1.4 (where the numbering is otherwise symmetric, R gets the lower locant: P-31.1.4.3.4).",
      "In the 3D view, the number button shows the same numbers, and the stereocenter button marks each stereo element.",
      "Each isomer is saved as SVG and XYZ in the isomers folder. 2D drawings with the same E/Z configuration share one layout, so only the wedges differ.",
      "Not handled in v0.1: axial chirality (atropisomers), planar chirality, and helicity."
    ],
